specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:29:- `cargo fmt -p agentix-qwen --check` passes. Workspace-wide formatting reports unrelated pre-existing diffs in voice and daemon files. Before the compatibility callback below, the focused tokenizer suite had one pass and two failures because MiniJinja 2.24.0 did not expose the `startswith` method used by the exact pinned chat template at line 93.
specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:34:- Kept the pinned MiniJinja 2.24.0 dependency and registered only the two string methods used by the pinned template through MiniJinja's unknown-method callback. After the edit, `nix develop --command cargo test -p agentix-qwen --test tokenizer` passed all three fixtures. Focused `cargo fmt -p agentix-qwen --check` and `cargo clippy -p agentix-qwen --all-targets -- -D warnings` also passed through Nix. These checks cover template rendering and the CPU crate only; no full model/backend is implemented.
specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:107:- Re-ran `nix develop --command cargo test --workspace`; it completed with exit 0, including the Qwen tokenizer and sys parser tests. `cargo fmt -p agentix-qwen -p agentix-qwen-sys --check` also passed. Workspace `cargo fmt --all --check` still reports formatting differences in existing voice/daemon files outside this feature.
specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:109:- The first combined Qwen Nix build failed because the new tokenizer module/tests were untracked and omitted from Nix's Git source. Staged those new source files, reran both Qwen package builds, and they completed with exit 0. `git diff --check` passed.
specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:115:- Added streaming SHA-256 file hashing and an explicit manifest digest verifier. `ModelIdentity` fingerprints canonicalize shard order and include config revision/hash, quantization, tokenizer/template hashes, optional MTP artifacts, and packing version. Focused tests cover hash correctness, digest match/mismatch, duplicate/invalid metadata, order stability, and sensitivity to each model-affecting identity input. Hashes are verified only when the caller invokes the file verifier; no checkpoint artifacts are present here.
specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:124:- Audited `cargo tree -p agentix-qwen --edges normal` and `cargo tree -p agentix-qwen-sys --edges normal`: the pure Qwen crate's runtime dependencies are MiniJinja, tokenizers, serde_json, and SHA-256; the native sys crate depends on the pinned `llama-cpp-sys-2` only. No Strata package appears in either tree. The Nix CUDA build path and worker binary/runtime isolation still require validation, so T007/T028 remain open.
specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:125:- Extended `quickstart.md` with the verified current dependency/package boundary, locked sys version, pinned tokenizer/template inputs, Nix CUDA capability mechanism (RTX 3090 target requires 8.6), and the limits of synthetic GGUF parser fixtures. T010 remains open because no architecture fixture/generator or final dependency review exists and CUDA is not built here.
specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:138:- Strengthened the pinned tokenizer fixture with an exact token-ID golden for the rendered `Hi!` user prompt and assistant thinking prefix: `[248045, 846, 198, 12675, 0, 248046, 198, 248045, 74455, 198, 248068, 198]`. IDs were captured by the existing Nix-pinned tokenizer/template artifacts, and the test continues to verify decode round-trip. Focused Qwen formatting, tests and Clippy passed. This closes only the simple prompt token case, not the full tokenizer/operator fixture task.
specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:139:- `nix build .#agentix-qwen --no-link` completed with exit 0 including the exact tokenizer ID golden; `git diff --check` passed.
specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:152:- Added checked context admission and `QwenTokenizer::prepare_prompt`, which renders with the pinned MiniJinja template, encodes the actual prompt, and admits the complete requested output bound against the configured context limit without truncating. Tests cover exact-fit, overflow, zero-output rejection, and tokenizer-derived token counts. Qwen formatting, all 40 Qwen tests, Clippy with warnings denied, workspace tests, and the Nix package build passed; lifecycle/generation wiring remains open.
specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:177:- Added a model-independent greedy generation controller: each step selects the finite maximum logit with lower-ID tie breaking, extends full context, and stops on tokenizer EOS/turn-end or the requested token limit. Tests cover tie behavior, stop without an extra logits call, zero limit, limits, and malformed logits. Focused formatter, sampler tests and Qwen Clippy pass. T020 remains partial because no model backend supplies logits and full-model decoding is unavailable.
specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:184:- Completed the coding-suite vocabulary documentation and dependency-boundary audit in `quickstart.md`: the pinned tokenizer represents 248,077 token IDs while the model embedding/output vocabulary is padded to 248,320 rows; the exact `cargo tree` commands show pure `agentix-qwen` has no GGML/GGUF native dependency, while `agentix-qwen-sys` owns GGUF parsing/row decoding through `llama-cpp-sys-2 0.1.154`. Both trees contain no Strata. The tokenizer values are confirmed by the checked tokenizer integration test, and the normal dependency trees were rerun after documenting them. The benchmark fixture remains draft because its baseline commit/evaluator are not yet available.
specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:185:- Added a public-opener integration test using a reduced valid Qwen config and two tiny indexed SafeTensors shards. It verifies that the opener derives row width, padded table size, source tensor names and numeric shard order from config, then routes the final row of one shard and first row of the next correctly. Focused test and strict Qwen Clippy pass. Full workspace formatting, tests, strict Clippy, both Qwen Nix package builds, tokenizer vocabulary acceptance search and `git diff --check` also pass after this addition.
specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:187:- Added an exhaustive n-gram boundary test over every model vocabulary token while history evolves. All 16 row IDs per token remain below the 320,001,446-row logical extent, confirming that the 90 extra physical PLE alignment rows cannot be addressed by n-gram hashing. The focused test completes in 0.09 seconds and Qwen all-target Clippy passes; the invariant and evidence are recorded in `qwen-design.md` and T018 notes.
specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:193:- Follow-up hardening added a cross-array validator for PLE multipliers/head offsets/vocabulary sizes, including odd multiplier and complete logical table extent checks. The first focused run fails in the synthetic metadata fixture because its hard-coded head ranges do not match the configured n-gram table extent. The failure is understood as fixture/validator disagreement; no code changes have been made after the failed run pending user direction. Latest green test/build evidence predates this validator change and does not cover the current tree.
specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:195:- Extended the source SafeTensors reader with bounded rank-two F32/F16/BF16 rows decoded to finite F32 values; rows share the existing bounded LRU store and report row/cache statistics. Added little-endian F16 conversion and synthetic tests for all three types, cache hits, shape/dtype rejection, and non-finite rejection. The focused storage suite (9 tests) and workspace format check pass. This adds the missing dense source row access primitive, while whole-tensor transformation and model-wide loading remain unimplemented. MiniJinja remains the tokenizer/template implementation as directed.
specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:201:- Added the Rust `build_benchmark_prompt_fixtures` example and generated deterministic 4,096/32,768/65,536-token rendered prompts from the Nix-pinned tokenizer/template. `fixtures/benchmark_prompts.json` records repeated-segment construction, rendered text, exact token IDs and little-endian ID hashes; two generator runs produced the same file SHA256 `c5a255bd4a271c3a14eebc762617dc511757dfa55b2019482d0d0075f021c939`. The tokenizer-backed integration test re-renders each prompt and verifies its exact IDs/hash. Generator and verifier pass through `nix develop`; Qwen/sys tests and strict all-target Clippy pass, formatting is clean, and the fixture's three token counts/ID-array lengths validate with `jq`. T009's prompt/token fixture portion is complete; its coding-task baseline/evaluator and benchmark execution remain open.
specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:254:- Extended the artifact sampler from the first QSA block through the remaining configured layers. A single actual token embedding now traverses all 48 blocks, including each recurrent/QSA state update, PLE at block 1, all attention/FFN residual mixers, all routed/shared MoE paths, final stream combine, and `output.weight`. The resulting 248,320 logits are finite; greedy token ID 79104 has logit 11.96474266. Refreshed evidence TSV SHA256: `fdf8b108f59530d135161a81e4bd447145300a1f13ebd2598b4f5fbf66214869`. This is a full one-token CPU forward smoke run, not independent expected-logit parity or a stateful generation/serving backend.
specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:256:- Added reusable `QwenGgufDecoder` over shared per-shard file handles and lazy tensor-row readers. It preserves all per-layer GatedDeltaNet/QSA caches, PLE n-gram/convolution state, and sequential position across calls; a failed partial step poisons the decoder rather than allowing corrupted state reuse. The IQ3_S full-model sampler now feeds token ID 1, selects greedy ID 79104, then feeds that token through a second complete 48-block step; both 248,320-value logits vectors are finite and the decoder reaches position 2, with second greedy ID 245228. The verified full sampler output is checked in; its refreshed evidence TSV SHA256 is recorded in the inventory JSON. This validates stateful two-token CPU execution, not an independent logit oracle.
specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:261:- Added the isolated `agentix-qwen-worker` package and exact-model daemon route, with full-shard SHA256 checks, model/tokenizer geometry checks before socket readiness, greedy chat completions and bounded SSE. MiniJinja remains the prompt-template renderer.
specs/021-strata-inference-research/implementation-log.md:267:- Hardened Qwen worker startup diagnostics after the deployed service reported an opaque `ENOENT`: missing/unreadable GGUF shards, config, tokenizer/template, socket directory, and socket bind now include the affected path. Focused worker tests pass (7 tests) in an isolated target directory, including exact missing-shard path reporting; formatting and `git diff --check` pass. The deployed log alone does not identify which path was missing, so shard absence remains the leading diagnosis rather than a proven cause.
