|---|---|---|
| agentix feature base | `fd2202890a95e1deb9747ccd8ad39be482f526f8` | Checkout and lockfile inspected |
| Strata | `7695859aa13afb248bdb4d36f9b2e95707db079d` | Clean detached checkout, CMake version 0.1.43 |
| Strata's ggml/llama.cpp dependency | `3cf03257f219afbe7334045ff7c6a06ac68c627d` | `CMakeLists.txt` FetchContent pin and `third_party/ggml/VERSION.txt`; dependency checkout not built |
| agentix 019 | `c96657c281e2ac74167b759a799b14a33e71f26e` | Ref recorded |
| agentix 020 | `0a70143265f7bb7eb83211cdd7caf11c4e7d7ced` | Inference/API contracts and changed-file inventory inspected |
| Full GSQ-RCO model | `ed59f92082b1e93c0e96d60a8b11aab089b52f09` | Strata setup pin confirmed with HF metadata |
| Coder GSQ-RCO model | `5348543e0147355ac9cbcb031184a3546350988e` | Strata setup pin confirmed with HF metadata |
| Unsloth candidate | `38bb39ee97821de2c9009abb7e93950eec396e66` | Strata setup pin; not selected for first experiment |
| Original Qwen MTP tensors | `de4b8e4d43b917e7706784d8bb445c9af86a3540` | `tools/mtp_fetch.py::PINNED_REVISION`, per-tensor SHA256 table |
| Qwen tokenizer | `de4b8e4d43b917e7706784d8bb445c9af86a3540` | `tokenizer.json`, pinned Nix hash `sha256-CZf0EMV6H05TsJ5L6PShctkO3ZVkNo+whHAwk3IpufM=`; addressable token count 248,077 |
| Qwen chat template | `de4b8e4d43b917e7706784d8bb445c9af86a3540` | `chat_template.jinja`, pinned Nix hash `sha256-w8+eNKv0+eNsLXIWWqnBMtPipyW2wlhqqjqK+deoEEE=`; three rendering fixtures pass with the MiniJinja compatibility callback |
| Qwen safetensors index | `de4b8e4d43b917e7706784d8bb445c9af86a3540` | Captured `model.safetensors.index.json` SHA256 `99e815241ef03325536b0aaa4441deea45174c17fae31e10f0bb456410c590de`; all 1,658 index name/shard assignments exactly match header-only reads across all 131 shards. Beyond the separately described PLE row, only small rank-one norm, `A_log`, and `dt_bias` payload samples have been fetched; no bulk payload was downloaded. |
| Qwen text source tensor headers | Same pinned Qwen revision | Range-read the 8-byte length prefix and complete SafeTensors JSON header (about 225 KiB total) from each of the 131 shards; no tensor payload was downloaded in this step. `evidence/qwen3_8_flash_next_text_tensor_headers.tsv` joins all 1,294 text checkpoint names to Agentix's source-to-GGUF mapping and records dtype, source shape, shard, and shard-local data offsets (SHA256 `53eaab9924d0626f1cf4f85de21f3709ccb4c21764cb33ac37618d70b5720a39`). The text tensors are 1,291 BF16 and three I64 PLE metadata vectors. Across all 1,658 header entries (including vision/MTP), every dtype/shape matches its declared byte range and all per-shard ranges are contiguous. `pinned_source_header_geometry_maps_to_complete_gguf_schema` checks every text source mapping/transform and proves its declared source geometry yields the complete 1,224-target GGUF schema geometry, including split, squeeze, and concatenated PLE shapes. Payload values remain unverified except for the specific PLE row and the direct norm/`A_log` vectors recorded separately. |
| Qwen norm and GatedDeltaNet source vector samples | Same pinned Qwen revision | Range-read a full 128-value BF16 linear-attention norm vector and 48-value BF16 layer-0 `A_log` and `dt_bias` vectors, plus their published F32 GGUF counterparts. The norm and `dt_bias` values match exactly after their direct transforms. The A-log values match within `1e-6` relative tolerance after `-exp` and head reorder. Offsets, hashes, limits and sample scope are recorded in `evidence/qwen3_8_flash_next_norm_vector_parity.json`, `evidence/qwen3_8_flash_next_alog_vector_parity.json`, and `evidence/qwen3_8_flash_next_dt_bias_vector_parity.json`. Tests wrap only these captured samples; no complete tensor payload was downloaded. |
| Rust SafeTensors metadata parser | crates.io `safetensors` 0.8.0, Apache-2.0 | Locked checksum `79b079b829cb27a1c3c374341345ed2e8b2c0c839034522cee576c140bd7f846`. Agentix deserializes bounded header JSON into the crate's public `Metadata`; its deserializer checks ranges and tensor shape/dtype byte sizes. The full file extent is independently checked before bounded row access. No unsafe mapping is used. |
| Qwen text source-to-GGUF name map | Same pinned Qwen and llama.cpp revisions | Agentix maps all 1,294 text-side index entries to metadata or GGUF names. The 1,224 unique targets equal the pinned Qwen schema and published shard header. Crosswalk: `evidence/qwen3_8_flash_next_source_to_gguf.tsv`, SHA256 `6ff72f51f99488cb2cfa7f7f7a1d7ede6841480cbeef3287ceb09dc8020ce7e0` (source tensor mapping list). It records PLE shard concatenation, indexer Q/K split, expert gate/up split, PLE norm offset/convolution squeeze, and GatedDeltaNet value-head reorder. The header-geometry integration test reconciles source dimensions for all text tensors with all target schema extents after those transforms. One norm and one A_log vector now have published-target value comparisons; most transformed payload values, quantized payloads and model loading remain unverified/unimplemented. Vision and MTP (364 index entries) are outside the text-only target. |
| Qwen PLE safetensors shard headers | Same pinned Qwen revision | Range-read the 8-byte prefix and complete JSON header for each of the 33 source shards containing PLE tensors. All 128 PLE tensors are BF16 `[2500012,160]`, yielding 320,001,536 rows of width 160 and 102,400,491,520 logical source bytes total. Evidence TSV: `evidence/qwen3_8_flash_next_ple_shard_headers.tsv`, SHA256 `d108021214b61a9fed86defb2bf25e963f3a03660f8856ab6eff351a4c9a3355`. These shapes and total rows match the published GGUF PLE extents `[160,320001536]` after GGUF dimension reversal. One row from `shard_0` is compared to published GGUF row 0 below. |
| Qwen source-to-published-GGUF PLE row parity | Same pinned Qwen revision and ggml-org GGUF revision `052beeaca7bec4a303e59cc7bc630c4f3a1b845d` | Range-read source BF16 row 0 (320 bytes, SHA256 `67354d4be4c2d2d8ed2f6003c5e98e56015072f08bbd5f62c6b38589628a35cb`) and GGUF Q4_0 row 0 (90 bytes, SHA256 `34098719c5d2b94c40150f2fbf5e04859571d27a1df605134e8deadb0d01cf73`). The new SafeTensors row reader obtains the source values; dequantized GGUF values match within max absolute error `0.003`. Evidence and exact limitations: `evidence/qwen3_8_flash_next_ple_row_parity.json`. This is one-row parity only. |
| Qwen non-PLE norm vector parity | Same pinned Qwen and ggml-org GGUF revisions above | Range-read the complete 256-byte BF16 source vector at source-file bytes `[110836296,110836551]` (tensor `model.language_model.layers.0.linear_attn.norm.weight`) and its 512-byte F32 target at GGUF-file bytes `[55842688,55843199]` (`blk.0.ssm_norm.weight`). Agentix's bounded SafeTensors vector reader and direct source transform match all 128 values exactly through the GGUF dense-row reader. Payload sample SHA256 values, tensor offsets, and the synthetic-reader test's scope are recorded in `evidence/qwen3_8_flash_next_norm_vector_parity.json`; the raw bytes are checked in beside it. This is one vector and does not verify complete shard payloads. |

